.TH geectl-request-file 1  "geectl-request-file 0.2.4" 
.SH NAME
geectl\-request\-file \- File a submit request: source package to a devel project, superseding every open submit request for the package from the same user
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgeectl request file\fR [\fB\-\-cve\fR] [\fB\-\-without\-cleanup\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-source\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-source\-package\fR> <\fB\-\-target\-project\fR> <\fB\-\-target\-package\fR> <\fB\-\-description\fR> <\fB\-\-changes\-entry\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
File a submit request: source package to a devel project, superseding every open submit request for the package from the same user
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-project\fR \fI<SOURCE_PROJECT>\fR
The project the change comes from (the branch)
.TP
\fB\-\-source\-package\fR \fI<SOURCE_PACKAGE>\fR
The package in the source project
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-project\fR \fI<TARGET_PROJECT>\fR
The project the request targets: the devel project, or openSUSE:Factory when the source is the recorded devel project and package
.TP
\fB\-\-target\-package\fR \fI<TARGET_PACKAGE>\fR
The package in the target project
.TP
\fB\-\-description\fR \fI<DESCRIPTION>\fR
The request description: one headline, then `\- ` lines for staging, needs, and rebuilds. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a description may open with a `\- ` bullet
.TP
\fB\-\-changes\-entry\fR \fI<CHANGES_ENTRY>\fR
The one `.changes` entry for this submission. It must name every CVE passed with `\-\-cve`. Values starting with `\-` are taken literally: a `.changes` entry starts with `\- `
.TP
\fB\-\-cve\fR \fI<CVE>\fR
A CVE this submission claims to fix. Repeatable; each one must be named in `\-\-changes\-entry`
.TP
\fB\-\-without\-cleanup\fR
Keep the source branch on accept instead of deleting it (cleanup is the default)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH VERSION
v0.2.4
